OL,3,CExcitement builds as South West
OL,4,Cprepares for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FIn Somerset, hundreds of people have
OL,8,Fclimbed up to the top of Glastonbury
OL,9,FTor to witness the once-in-a-
OL,10,Fgeneration event.
OL,12,FAs the most dramatic solar eclipse in
OL,13,Fdecades got underway, one skygazer
OL,14,Fshared her memories of being at the
OL,15,Ftop of the Tor for the total solar
OL,16,Feclipse in 1999.
OL,18,FShe said: "I was here with my sisters,
OL,19,Fwe were teenagers at the time, and my
OL,20,FDad.
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G4/9
OL,2,W,.!+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BSW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,403,400,120,260,000,100
PN,40205
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F402A1786560487
OL,3,CExcitement builds as South West
OL,4,Cprepares for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,F"So it's really nice to be back here
OL,8,Fwith my sisters, their children, and
OL,9,Fmy Dad whose ashes are still on this
OL,10,FTor today."
OL,12,FShe added: "There's just something
OL,13,Fspecial about Glastonbury, we love
OL,14,Fcoming to Glastonbury. It's a special
OL,15,Fplace for us, as I'm sure it's a
OL,16,Fspecial place for lots of people."
OL,18,FHundreds of people have climbed up to
OL,19,Fthe top of Glastonbury Tor to watch
OL,20,Fthe solar eclipse, as ITV News' Nick
OL,21,FSmith reports
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G5/9
